  {
   "uuid": "acf3c8f6-d4f3-42e3-8760-1a0611c5739b",
   "text": "",
   "content": [
    {
     "start_timestamp": "2026-05-24T20:23:22.106000Z",
     "stop_timestamp": "2026-05-24T20:23:38.773000Z",
     "type": "text",
     "text": "At 0.75%, yes, most likely both. You can try a new chain alone first: if it skips on the middle cogs under load, the cassette is worn and you'll need to replace it too. For 105 11-speed, a CS-R7000 cassette and an HG601/HG701 chain are standard replacements. Then re-check cable tension after installing; new parts sometimes need a quarter turn.",
     "citations": []
    }
   ],
